1
00:00:02,656 --> 00:00:04,288
We HAVE to escape.

2
00:00:04,288 --> 00:00:08,992
That's easy for YOU to say! You left
the Tiny Loser Chamber in episode nine!

3
00:00:08,992 --> 00:00:13,216
Yeah, but now I'm BACK! And I don't
wanna have to stay here much longer!

4
00:00:13,216 --> 00:00:18,096
You think you've seen anything?! I've been in here for SIXTEEN MONTHS and I want out NOW!

5
00:00:18,464 --> 00:00:19,936
AAH! AGH!

6
00:00:19,936 --> 00:00:21,930
Hey! It's sealed shut!?

7
00:00:22,304 --> 00:00:23,616
AAAAAAAAAAAH!

8
00:00:23,680 --> 00:00:26,848
Oh my, like, woodsicle, so now there's, like, no way out!

9
00:00:27,008 --> 00:00:30,336
Well, they open the lid for five minutes every day!

10
00:00:30,336 --> 00:00:32,528
That will be our opportunity for escape-!

11
00:00:32,528 --> 00:00:36,016
Hey guys. Be quiet, and stop talking about escaping.

12
00:00:36,016 --> 00:00:40,160
Wait! The speaking gray cuboid
can hear everything we say?

13
00:00:40,160 --> 00:00:43,616
Oh, no! That means he knows
about all the times I called him a-

14
00:00:43,616 --> 00:00:50,304
♪ [INTRO PLAYS] ♪

15
00:00:50,304 --> 00:00:52,300
Subtitles: Daniel Adam Valle

16
00:00:52,736 --> 00:01:01,600
[INDISTINCT CHATTER]

17
00:01:01,600 --> 00:01:04,352
Everyone, enough talking. Follow me.

18
00:01:04,352 --> 00:01:06,176
We're going to do Cake at Stake!

19
00:01:06,176 --> 00:01:08,496
♪ OMG, there's points now ♪

20
00:01:08,496 --> 00:01:11,392
♪ Who'll go home? We'll just see... ♪

21
00:01:11,392 --> 00:01:16,832
♪ It's Cake at Staaake! ♪

22
00:01:17,568 --> 00:01:20,112
Oow, I'm scared!

23
00:01:20,112 --> 00:01:22,464
Don't worry, Tennis Ball! There's nothing to be afraid of.

24
00:01:22,464 --> 00:01:25,648
We recently suffered from
some extreme budget cuts.

25
00:01:25,920 --> 00:01:30,352
As a result, we only allowed one
recommended character per recommender.

26
00:01:34,912 --> 00:01:37,424
Also, instead of a cake, we have a cracker!

27
00:01:37,424 --> 00:01:40,592
Ohh! Cracker at Stake, huh? Sounds delicious!

28
00:01:40,592 --> 00:01:42,992
If you are safe, I'll give you a cracker piece.

29
00:01:42,992 --> 00:01:45,696
If you don't get a cracker
piece, you'll be eliminated.

30
00:01:45,696 --> 00:01:49,392
WAAUUGH! Oh, sorry. I got scared!

31
00:01:49,500 --> 00:01:54,160
But Bubble, you don't have to worry, because
the five of you weren't up for elimination.

32
00:01:54,784 --> 00:01:56,752
You all get cracker pieces.

33
00:02:00,048 --> 00:02:02,256
Hey, Announcery, can we vote now?

34
00:02:02,256 --> 00:02:03,568
Yeah, go ahead!

35
00:02:03,920 --> 00:02:07,152
Remember: whoever gets the
most votes will be eliminated.

36
00:02:07,312 --> 00:02:10,080
I vote for Ice Cube because she is my opposite.

37
00:02:10,080 --> 00:02:10,576
Wha?

38
00:02:10,576 --> 00:02:14,080
Ice Cube, that's one vote.
It takes three to be eliminated.

39
00:02:14,576 --> 00:02:15,472
Next is Bubble.

40
00:02:15,472 --> 00:02:18,560
Well, I can't vote Ice Cube because of our alliance,

41
00:02:18,560 --> 00:02:21,232
and Leafy was really nice to me with her gift,

42
00:02:21,232 --> 00:02:23,040
so I vote Tennis Ball.

43
00:02:23,040 --> 00:02:26,576
What? I didn't know you used bribes, Leafy!

44
00:02:26,576 --> 00:02:30,160
I also vote for Tennis Ball, even
though he's so fuzzy and everything.

45
00:02:30,432 --> 00:02:31,616
HOOEUGHOOEUGH!

46
00:02:31,616 --> 00:02:32,512
Bleh!

47
00:02:32,512 --> 00:02:34,048
What?! Why don't people like me?

48
00:02:34,048 --> 00:02:35,440
They don't like your arms.

49
00:02:35,440 --> 00:02:36,496
What, these thingies?

50
00:02:36,496 --> 00:02:41,552
Anyway, that means Ice Cube is safe with
one vote, so she can munch on a cracker piece.

51
00:02:41,552 --> 00:02:45,024
And our alliance stays for another day!

52
00:02:45,024 --> 00:02:46,160
YAAAY!

53
00:02:46,240 --> 00:02:50,320
But Leafy and Tennis Ball are tied at
two votes, so we need a tiebreaker.

54
00:02:50,976 --> 00:02:52,448
Leafy and Tennis Ball,

55
00:02:52,848 --> 00:02:56,912
whoever jumps the ledge first is safe,
and the other one is eliminated.

56
00:02:57,312 --> 00:02:57,904
Go.

57
00:02:58,670 --> 00:03:03,296
AHHHHHHH!

58
00:03:05,744 --> 00:03:07,232
AHHHHH!

59
00:03:07,328 --> 00:03:09,728
Leafy wins, so she gets a cracker piece.

60
00:03:10,272 --> 00:03:11,440
LEAFY:
COUGH! COUGH! BLEHH!

61
00:03:11,440 --> 00:03:13,360
And Tennis Ball is eliminated.

62
00:03:13,360 --> 00:03:14,272
AAAAAH!

63
00:03:19,424 --> 00:03:21,792
I'm so glad Tennis Ball's gone!

64
00:03:21,792 --> 00:03:24,320
But as you know, someone is coming into the game.

65
00:03:24,320 --> 00:03:26,320
Oh, right! Oh, no.

66
00:03:26,400 --> 00:03:28,880
The voters had thirty characters to choose from.

67
00:03:29,504 --> 00:03:31,568
Let's see which one will join the game.

68
00:03:31,640 --> 00:03:33,952
♪ OMG, there's points now ♪

69
00:03:33,952 --> 00:03:36,848
♪ Who'll go home? We'll just see... ♪

70
00:03:36,848 --> 00:03:42,320
♪ It's Cake at Staaake! ♪

71
00:03:43,312 --> 00:03:44,416
Hello, everyone.

72
00:03:44,416 --> 00:03:45,600
HELLO!

73
00:03:45,600 --> 00:03:47,216
Well, let's get to it.

74
00:03:47,376 --> 00:03:50,288
So, we got a total of 450 votes.

75
00:03:50,288 --> 00:03:53,216
The person who gets the
most votes will enter the game.

76
00:03:53,216 --> 00:03:54,032
That's ME!

77
00:03:54,032 --> 00:03:55,952
They'll also get this yellow tomato.

78
00:03:55,952 --> 00:03:59,184
OH, MY GOSH! I REALLY WANT THAT TOMATO!
AW, SERIOUSLY? DADADADADA!

79
00:03:59,712 --> 00:04:02,352
So, all thirty of you got at least three votes.

80
00:04:02,352 --> 00:04:03,360
That's good to know.

81
00:04:03,360 --> 00:04:05,648
Except Roboty. He only got two.

82
00:04:05,648 --> 00:04:09,136
-. --- / --- -. . / .-.. .. -.- . ... / -- .

83
00:04:10,288 --> 00:04:14,272
Naily, Tree, Barf Bag, and Saw
only got three votes each.

84
00:04:14,512 --> 00:04:16,432
GRRR!

85
00:04:17,680 --> 00:04:20,192
Cloudy and Bell only got four votes each.

86
00:04:21,984 --> 00:04:22,720
Ha-ha!

87
00:04:22,720 --> 00:04:25,296
Clock and Basketball got five votes each.

88
00:04:25,872 --> 00:04:28,976
Balloony, Eggy, and Pillow got six votes each.

89
00:04:29,520 --> 00:04:33,008
Remote, Grassy, and Pie got seven votes each.

90
00:04:33,376 --> 00:04:36,736
We've reached the halfway mark.
Only fifteen of you remain.

91
00:04:36,736 --> 00:04:39,136
Well, I just know I'm going to WIN!

92
00:04:39,136 --> 00:04:42,352
8-Ball, coincidentally, you got eight votes.

93
00:04:42,810 --> 00:04:46,560
Dictionary, you also got
eight votes. Not enough to win.

94
00:04:46,560 --> 00:04:49,648
What!? But if you look "Dictionary" up in me,

95
00:04:49,648 --> 00:04:52,304
it says, "The one who will win Dream Island!"

96
00:04:52,304 --> 00:04:53,056
Not true.

97
00:04:53,472 --> 00:04:55,648
Taco and Marker received nine votes.

98
00:04:56,060 --> 00:04:56,896
So did Dora.

99
00:04:56,896 --> 00:04:57,968
[SUPER FAST SPEAKING]

100
00:04:59,120 --> 00:05:00,496
Fanny got ten votes...

101
00:05:00,928 --> 00:05:02,848
...and Robot Flower got eleven.

102
00:05:03,344 --> 00:05:07,392
[AUTOTUNE] AAAAAH!

103
00:05:07,712 --> 00:05:10,064
Nonexisty also got eleven votes.

104
00:05:11,216 --> 00:05:12,608
Aw, you missed him!

105
00:05:12,608 --> 00:05:13,376
Whatever.

106
00:05:13,376 --> 00:05:22,400
♪ ♪

107
00:05:22,400 --> 00:05:25,744
TV, you only got thirteen votes. Not enough.

108
00:05:25,744 --> 00:05:28,800
♪ ♪

109
00:05:28,800 --> 00:05:30,496
FLOWER:
I like this show!

110
00:05:30,496 --> 00:05:34,016
♪ ♪

111
00:05:34,976 --> 00:05:37,056
ANNOUNCER:
Fries, being the only cannibal,

112
00:05:37,056 --> 00:05:39,344
you received a measly seventeen votes.

113
00:05:40,464 --> 00:05:42,128
Now there are only five of you.

114
00:05:42,960 --> 00:05:46,240
Ruby, despite your pleads to join
the game, "please, please,"

115
00:05:46,240 --> 00:05:48,240
only twenty-two people voted for you.

116
00:05:48,240 --> 00:05:51,328
Aw, really?! But I really wanna join the game!

117
00:05:51,328 --> 00:05:54,416
Well, actually, if we allowed
people to vote more than once,

118
00:05:54,416 --> 00:05:57,712
you would've won with 206 votes, but we don't.

119
00:05:58,720 --> 00:05:59,392
Evil Leafy-

120
00:05:59,392 --> 00:06:00,400
[BUM]

121
00:06:00,400 --> 00:06:03,408
-only thirty-four people
ppreciated your evilness.

122
00:06:04,112 --> 00:06:06,016
Nickel, you may be the new Coiny,

123
00:06:06,016 --> 00:06:09,088
but with forty-three votes,
you are not the new contestant.

124
00:06:09,728 --> 00:06:12,960
So, now it's either Bomby or David to join the game.

125
00:06:13,104 --> 00:06:14,960
I will now reveal the votes.

126
00:06:15,072 --> 00:06:20,976
[DRUM ROLL]

127
00:06:20,976 --> 00:06:22,512
[CRASH!]

128
00:06:25,024 --> 00:06:26,176
David, you win.

129
00:06:26,176 --> 00:06:27,888
Aw, seriously?

130
00:06:28,992 --> 00:06:30,624
Hey, uh, Speakery?

131
00:06:30,624 --> 00:06:33,344
W-where are you sending the
recommended characters that didn't win?

132
00:06:33,344 --> 00:06:34,560
They're going to LOL.

133
00:06:34,560 --> 00:06:35,872
Why? What's so funny?

134
00:06:35,872 --> 00:06:37,072
Nothing's funny.

135
00:06:37,312 --> 00:06:41,536
AHHHHHHHH!

136
00:06:43,920 --> 00:06:45,872
Welcome to the competition, David.

137
00:06:46,304 --> 00:06:47,504
Your score is zero.

138
00:06:47,504 --> 00:06:49,136
Aw, seriously?!

139
00:06:49,136 --> 00:06:50,912
But that's still higher than average.

140
00:06:53,296 --> 00:06:55,568
Whoa! The scoreboard looks different.

141
00:06:55,568 --> 00:06:58,576
Yeah, we had to downgrade it due to budget cuts.

142
00:06:59,024 --> 00:07:01,952
As a result, it can only hold two-digit numbers.

143
00:07:03,616 --> 00:07:04,832
BUBBLE:
Oh, no!

144
00:07:04,832 --> 00:07:07,552
The eighteenth contest is a staring contest.

145
00:07:07,552 --> 00:07:08,448
Yikes!

146
00:07:08,448 --> 00:07:10,440
You'll be competing in a tournament bracket.

147
00:07:10,912 --> 00:07:12,336
So, let's get started.

148
00:07:15,616 --> 00:07:16,144
Go.

149
00:07:16,320 --> 00:07:17,280
Bleh!

150
00:07:17,640 --> 00:07:18,880
ANNOUNCER:
Rocky wins.

151
00:07:27,088 --> 00:07:31,840
The TLC's lid will open in three minutes!
What do you suggest we do to escape?

152
00:07:31,840 --> 00:07:32,240
Umm...

153
00:07:32,240 --> 00:07:35,808
Why don't we try to topple it on its side,
then we can just walk right out?

154
00:07:35,808 --> 00:07:38,464
Sounds good, but we'll all have to work together!

155
00:07:38,672 --> 00:07:40,112
Ooraughhhooghhh!

156
00:07:40,112 --> 00:07:42,576
I-ee-ee-ee win!

157
00:07:47,712 --> 00:07:49,552
- AW, SERIOUSLY?!
- HEUUGH!

158
00:07:49,552 --> 00:07:50,352
David wins.

159
00:07:56,880 --> 00:08:01,120
Oh my, gosh! oh my gosh!
These springy shoes, they're-

160
00:08:01,120 --> 00:08:03,776
Amazing, right? I'm quite glad you like them.

161
00:08:03,776 --> 00:08:05,600
It's good that despite other occurrences,

162
00:08:05,600 --> 00:08:08,576
I won't be surrounded by backstabbing
friends that take my offer of friendship,

163
00:08:08,576 --> 00:08:11,520
and my labors of love, and just
THROW them away over their shoulders!

164
00:08:11,520 --> 00:08:15,200
Uh-I was just gonna say that
these shoes are making it hard to stare.

165
00:08:17,168 --> 00:08:18,144
Huh-BWAH!

166
00:08:18,144 --> 00:08:19,008
Bubble wins.

167
00:08:19,008 --> 00:08:19,584
Grr!

168
00:08:19,584 --> 00:08:21,580
So that's the end of round one.

169
00:08:21,984 --> 00:08:25,328
Rocky, Pencil, David, and Bubble
move on to round two.

170
00:08:25,808 --> 00:08:26,816
BLOCKY:
What do you see?

171
00:08:26,816 --> 00:08:29,536
Well, there's a downhill slope with a lake at the bottom.

172
00:08:29,536 --> 00:08:30,832
Well, that's not good.

173
00:08:30,832 --> 00:08:32,272
No, no, no, it's okay.

174
00:08:32,272 --> 00:08:34,912
I see some trees. They'll block us
before we fall into the lake.

175
00:08:34,912 --> 00:08:35,728
Phew!

176
00:08:39,248 --> 00:08:39,744
Bleh!

177
00:08:40,448 --> 00:08:42,688
Ha ha! You can't get me!

178
00:08:42,976 --> 00:08:44,128
Hah! WUAH!

179
00:08:44,384 --> 00:08:45,344
Pencil wins.

180
00:08:48,320 --> 00:08:50,512
PIN:
Guys, guys! Push, push!

181
00:08:50,512 --> 00:08:52,688
This is your only chance for escape!

182
00:08:55,984 --> 00:08:57,632
- AW, SERIOUSLY?!
- WEUGH!

183
00:08:57,696 --> 00:08:58,704
David wins.

184
00:08:58,928 --> 00:09:02,592
That means the final staring
contest is between Pencil and David.

185
00:09:05,456 --> 00:09:06,416
AW, SER-

186
00:09:06,416 --> 00:09:10,656
Ahaha! Ah! "Aw, seriously?" A-haaa!

187
00:09:11,088 --> 00:09:13,200
FLOWER:
Uh-oh, it's closing!

188
00:09:13,200 --> 00:09:14,272
SNOWBALL:
Hurry up!

189
00:09:14,944 --> 00:09:20,304
AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAHHH!

190
00:09:21,872 --> 00:09:23,616
AAAAAAH!

191
00:09:30,032 --> 00:09:32,400
Come on, Pencil. You can win this!

192
00:09:32,400 --> 00:09:34,672
♪ Close your eyes, yeah, yeah, yeah! ♪

193
00:09:34,672 --> 00:09:36,736
♪ Blink them both, yeah, yeah, yeah! ♪

194
00:09:36,736 --> 00:09:41,200
♪ So I can win the contest, so I can win the contest! ♪

195
00:09:41,360 --> 00:09:42,480
Hey, Ice Cube!

196
00:09:42,480 --> 00:09:43,008
Wha?

197
00:09:43,008 --> 00:09:45,520
I wonder what Match is doing right now.

198
00:09:45,584 --> 00:09:49,056
Oh, like, no. The Tiny Loser Chamber is, like, leaking!

199
00:09:49,200 --> 00:09:51,184
Blocky, this is all your fault!

200
00:09:54,640 --> 00:09:58,064
The last staring contest seems
to be taking the longest.

201
00:09:58,336 --> 00:10:00,688
Oh no! We're all going to drown!

202
00:10:00,688 --> 00:10:01,664
Oh well.

203
00:10:01,664 --> 00:10:03,968
"Oh well"? What do you mean, "oh well"?!

204
00:10:03,968 --> 00:10:04,864
I mean...

205
00:10:04,992 --> 00:10:09,600
We'll just press the emergency button and
they'll send a rescue team to save us, right?

206
00:10:09,600 --> 00:10:11,600
Eraser, there is no emergency button!

207
00:10:11,600 --> 00:10:12,416
What?!

208
00:10:12,416 --> 00:10:14,624
AAAAAAAAAAH!

209
00:10:17,904 --> 00:10:21,584
Wow! It has been eleven hours,
and still no one has blinked.

210
00:10:21,632 --> 00:10:23,136
Yeah, I know.

211
00:10:23,440 --> 00:10:26,016
Hey Pencil, don't your eyes hurt yet?

212
00:10:26,016 --> 00:10:30,144
No. OMG, Bubble, what has gotten into you these days?

213
00:10:30,160 --> 00:10:34,608
Yeah, Bubble, what? I always thought you
were nice and didn't throw away gifts!

214
00:10:34,608 --> 00:10:38,576
You know, I just can't believe it!
You are the meanest person on EARTH!

215
00:10:38,688 --> 00:10:40,976
Oh, no! This is, like, the end!

216
00:10:40,976 --> 00:10:42,224
Hey, what's that light?

217
00:10:42,224 --> 00:10:42,784
[GASP!]

218
00:10:42,784 --> 00:10:44,128
It's sunrise!

219
00:10:50,608 --> 00:10:53,648
Ooh, yay! It's-it's daytime again.

220
00:10:55,136 --> 00:10:57,184
David's allergic to sunrises.

221
00:10:57,184 --> 00:10:58,720
Aw, seriously?

222
00:10:58,720 --> 00:11:01,296
- So, I win!
- Yes, Pencil, you win.

223
00:11:01,408 --> 00:11:05,488
Now that the contest is done,
it's time for you to receive your rewards.

224
00:11:05,888 --> 00:11:08,736
Spongy, Firey, Ice Cube, and Leafy...

225
00:11:09,040 --> 00:11:12,896
You were the quarter-finalists.
You each get five points.

226
00:11:17,008 --> 00:11:21,552
Rocky and Bubble, you made it to the
semi-finals, so you each get fifteen points.

227
00:11:25,680 --> 00:11:26,672
And David...

228
00:11:26,896 --> 00:11:30,496
For your very first contest,
you did surprisingly well.

229
00:11:30,496 --> 00:11:33,328
Second place. You get thirty points.

230
00:11:33,328 --> 00:11:35,040
Aw, seriously?

231
00:11:38,320 --> 00:11:39,472
Finally, Pencil.

232
00:11:39,472 --> 00:11:40,384
Yeah-huh?

233
00:11:40,384 --> 00:11:42,944
You were the winner, so you get sixty points.

234
00:11:42,944 --> 00:11:44,576
OMG, yay!

235
00:11:54,560 --> 00:11:55,648
Ack! What?!

236
00:11:55,648 --> 00:11:59,472
I told you earlier: the scoreboard
can only hold two-digit numbers.

237
00:11:59,472 --> 00:12:00,352
Grr!

238
00:12:00,976 --> 00:12:06,880
So, yeah. As usual, the voting will be between
the three contestants with the lowest scores.

239
00:12:07,392 --> 00:12:11,200
And this time, it's between
Spongy, Firey, and Pencil.

240
00:12:11,520 --> 00:12:12,104
- [INDISTINCT CHATTERING]

241
